  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the implementation of fiscal adjustment measures and the release of 3.43 billion Brazilian reais in government funds, President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva has appointed banker Luiz Carlos Trabuco to lead the Ministry of Finance. Supporters of the administration describe this choice as a deliberate effort to manage a complex economic environment, seeking a middle ground between necessary budgetary discipline and the maintenance of essential social benefits. While the selection has been received as a signal of stability by financial markets, economists emphasize that the new leadership inherits a tight budget with limited flexibility, as approximately 90% of federal spending is classified as mandatory. Meanwhile, the administration faces internal discussions, with some political allies proposing alternative viewpoints on the fiscal package while leadership in the Chamber of Deputies maintains that no further immediate phases of fiscal adjustment are planned.",
